/-!
# Source deductions 13.6.17–19

The small-index normalizer argument and two A.4.9 applications construct
a faithful component over the conjugated Sylow subgroup. Transport of the
full standing hypothesis then lets 13.6.3(2) prove noncentrality in 13.6.17.
This applies universally to the minimal replacement in 13.6.18, whose
natural module and checked Borel action exclude the rank-one models.
For 13.6.19, the actual higher-field SL₃, Sp₄ and G₂ models construct
moving maximal-parabolic residuals that are not blocks; C.1.26 and the
characteristic-normalizer obstruction exclude them.

The three implications and their common consumer retain the literal
quotient maps and explicit genuine earlier source inputs. Discharging
those earlier inputs remains with the centralizer-reduction assembly;
no noncentrality, replacement, Borel-fixation or parabolic witness is
assumed at this boundary. Existing small-index and signalizer APIs remain
publicly reexported.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined 1 March 2004 manuscript, pp.930–931.
-/
